ss><country>JP</country> </address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAKOSHI NOBUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIDEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINDENGEN ELECTRIC MFG</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUI, MASANORI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAKOSHI, NOBUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIDEYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINDENGEN ELECTRIC MANUFACTURING CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUI MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAKOSHI NOBUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA HIDEYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUI, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAKOSHI, NOBUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, HIDEYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A heavily doped region (18) forming a surface part of a drain layer (2) of a first conductivity type is diffused more deeply than a main diffused layer (36) and a diffused channel layer (37) so that it may have a low resistivity.  This heavily doped region (18) is enclosed by a diffused region (40) of a second conductivity type composed of a diffused base layer (38) and a diffused guard ring layer (13).  Therefore, the heavily doped region (18) does not form a spherical joint, and a depletion layer spreading in the heavily doped region (18) expands into the heavily doped region (18).  Therefore, high dielectric strength is provided while low resistivity is maintained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon l'invention, une région fortement dopée (18) formant une partie superficielle d'une couche de drain (2) d'un premier type de conductivité est diffusée plus profondément qu'une couche principale diffusée (36) ou une couche de canal diffusée (37), ce qui lui confère une faible résistivité. Cette région fortement dopée (18) est cernée par une région diffusée (40) d'un second type de conductivité constituée d'une couche de support diffusée (38) et d'une couche à anneau de garde diffusée (13). Ainsi, la région fortement dopée (18) ne forme pas un joint sphérique, et une couche de déplétion étalée dans la région fortement dopée (18) s'étend à l'intérieur de ladite région (18). Le dispositif acquiert ainsi une rigidité diélectrique élevée tout en conservant sa faible résistivité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>